    {
      "text": "A Roman handshake became a ring.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Romans made rings with two clasped right hands.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Right hands",
        "sub": "Roman rings",
        "piece": "ring",
        "stone": "sapphire",
        "cut": "oval",
        "metal": "yellow"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The right hand was sacred to Fides, the goddess of good faith.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "ring",
        "stone": "ruby",
        "cut": "cushion",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Fides, goddess of good faith"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Medieval goldsmiths brought the design back in the 12th century.",
      "say": "Medieval goldsmiths brought the design back in the twelfth century.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "12th century",
        "sub": "Goldsmiths revive it",
        "piece": "brooch",
        "stone": "ruby",
        "cut": "round",
        "petals": 8,
        "metal": "yellow"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Betrothal rings often took the form of clasped hands.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "317-a-roman-handshake-became-a-ring-0.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "A Renaissance fede ring",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The name fede comes from Italian, mani in fede, hands in faith.",
      "say": "The name fay-day comes from Italian, MAH-nee in fay-day, hands in faith.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Mani in fede",
        "sub": "Hands in faith",
        "piece": "eternity",
        "stone": "diamond",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "stones": 16
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Some rings had two hoops, one worn by each partner.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "band",
        "metal": "rose",
        "label": "Two hoops"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "At the wedding the two hoops were joined into one ring.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "eternity",
        "stone": "diamond",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "stones": 14,
        "label": "One ring again"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The Claddagh ring is a fede ring with a heart and crown.",
      "say": "The KLAD-uh ring is a fay-day ring with a heart and crown.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "ring",
        "stone": "emerald",
        "cut": "heart",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "The Irish Claddagh"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The clasped hands stayed popular on rings until the 1800s.",
      "say": "The clasped hands stayed popular on rings until the eighteen hundreds.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "317-a-roman-handshake-became-a-ring-1.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "A sixth century gold ring",
