      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "caption": "The fede ring shows two clasped hands, a design that began with the Romans. Its name comes from the Italian mani in fede, hands in faith. Medieval goldsmiths brought it back in the 12th century, Renaissance couples used it for betrothals, and the Irish Claddagh ring is a fede ring with a heart and crown.",
